ion.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "258962"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "308124"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "356837"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19001870"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/701"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "BMX, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "1 –  2 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2178"} "Vélodrome de Saint-Quentin-en-Yvelines, Montigny-le-Bretonneux, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2003620"} "24 from 17 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The men’s BMX racing final at Paris 2024 proceeded under favourable weather conditions, and the presence of French President Emmanuel Macron added to the celebratory atmosphere."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This was a landmark event for France, as the host nation achieved a historic podium sweep at the Saint-Quentin-en-Yvelines BMX stadium. " [:a {:href "/athletes/125019"} "Joris Daudet"] " secured gold with a time of 31.422 seconds, followed closely by " [:a {:href "/athletes/142843"} "Sylvain André"] " (31.706) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/142842"} "Romain Mahieu"] " (32.022)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This podium sweep marked a significant turnaround for the French team, who had faced disappointment at Tokyo 2020 where none of the trio reached the podium. For three-time World champion Daudet, the gold medal was particularly meaningful, as it was his first Olympic medal in four appearances."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The race was not without incident. Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/143121"} "Kye Whyte"] ", the silver medalist from Tokyo 2020, suffered a heavy crash during the semifinals and was removed from the track by stretcher, while Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/151388"} "Izaac Kennedy"] ", a strong medal contender, crashed on the first turn, eliminating his chances for a medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Missing from the Paris 2024 final were two Tokyo 2020 medalists. Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/135246"} "Niek Kimmann"] " (NED) failed to qualify for the event, and bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/133260"} "Carlos Ramírez"] " (COL), also the Rio 2016 bronze medalist, finished 20th in the semifinals and did not advance."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Last Run Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/125019"} "Joris Daudet"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "Final Round"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "31.422"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/142843"} "Sylvain André"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "Final Round"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "31.706"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "100"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/142842"} "Romain Mahieu"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazona